  "result": "I fixed the \"Load more\" paging bug in `src/server/repositories/_paging.ts`. I haven't run the test suite or paged through a real list.\n\nThe cause was that the cursor predicate only asked for rows strictly older than the last row shown. Rows created at the same moment, as in a bulk import, were skipped once one of them ended a page. It now also keeps rows with the same timestamp and a smaller id. That matches the existing sort order (timestamp, then id, both descending).\n\nThe predicate is shared, so the same change covers the project issue list, notification inbox, audit log, and the comment, member, project and search lists. Every list query already filters by workspace, so paging doesn't pull in another workspace's entries.",
